<title>USA: USDA plans continued cotton ginning survey.</title>
<headline>USDA plans continued cotton ginning survey.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department said Tuesday it wanted to extend the agency's cotton ginning survey, and asked for public comment on its plan.</p>
<p>In a notice published in the Federal Register, the agency's National Agricultural Statistics Service said public comments must be received by Sept. 11.</p>
<p>The USDA's cotton ginning survey collects information from some 11,600 industry respondents for specific dates and geographic regions, and helps in forecasting U.S. cotton production.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
</text>
